{"name":"Black Rooster","hex":"#331111","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"rooster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male domestic chicken (Gallus gallus domesticus) or other gallinaceous bird.","A bird or bat which roosts or is roosting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rooster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black Rooster (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Rooster EP is the debut EP by indie rock band The Kills."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/The_Kills_-_Black_Rooster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Rooster_(EP)","wikidata":"Q4921745"},{"title":"Chicken","blocks":[{"text":"The chicken is the domesticated form of the red junglefowl, originally native to Southeast Asia. It was first domesticated around 8,000 years ago and is one of the most common and widespread domesticated animals in the world. Chickens are primarily kept for their meat and eggs, though they are also kept as pets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_chicken_sitting_together.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken","wikidata":"Q780"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif/lossy-page1-500px-GLW_2_global_distributions_of_c%29_chickens.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGLW_2_global_distributions_of_c)_chickens.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Rooster_portrait2.jpg/500px-Rooster_portrait2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Rooster_portrait2.jpg/1280px-Rooster_portrait2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Rooster_portrait2.jpg/500px-Rooster_portrait2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont